WEBVTT

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:03.650
Yusei!

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:04.970
Yusei!

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:04.970
Bro!

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:13.890
I'll soon send you back to that 
garbage dump you call a hometown!

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:16.780
But I'm going to kill you first!

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:21.710
Stand up!

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:23.340
Bro!

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:25.370
Yusei.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:53.390
No matter how far apart we 
are, we can't be stopped

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:58.390
That's deeply engraved into us

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:06.880
So don't be afraid of getting hurt

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:12.890
Break through even further

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:18.400
While carrying you beliefs in your heart

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:25.550
There's always only one truth

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:29.440
So feel the voice of your heart

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:34.230
With your unwavering emotions

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:40.330
Seize the signs of tomorrow

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:16.390
Deck 0 
Break the Chain Trap Loop

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:37.660
That's the spirit.

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:42.430
If it ends now, the duel isn't worth it.

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:48.720
That punk is confident because electricity 
doesn't flow through his Duel Disk.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.190
My turn.

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:55.860
From my hand, I activate the 
spell card Nightmare's Steelcage.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:06.220
When this card activates, all monsters 
cannot attack for two turns.

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:09.280
You can't even summon a monster?

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:12.750
I set one card and end my turn.

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:16.730
All right!  My card saved Yusei from trouble!

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:19.810
You fool!  He's still in trouble!

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:21.640
My turn!

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:31.270
You believe that you can prevent damage with 
Steelcage, but will that actually come true?

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:34.920
Appear, Iron Chain Snake!

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:40.050
Then due to Iron Chain 
Repairman's monster effect,

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:43.610
I Special Summon a Level 
4-or-below Chain Monster!

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:46.260
Resurrect, Iron Chain Snake!

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.820
I activate two Continuous Spells!

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:55.850
With Poison Chain, if I didn't 
battle during the turn,

00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:59.380
the opponent sends cards in 
his deck to the graveyard

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:01.330
equal to the total Level 
of my Chain Monsters.

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:09.220
My total monster Level is 10!  Therefore, 
you send ten cards in your deck to the graveyard!

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:11.730
What?

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:15.490
You built that deck using 
cards from those losers.

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:17.470
Garbage will always be garbage.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:20.250
Hurry up and go to the graveyard.

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:29.900
Now your deck has 19 cards remaining.

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:33.980
I see.  His real target 
is to destroy his deck.

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:38.430
If he discards 10 cards per turn, then 
Yusei's deck won't last two turns.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:42.390
The effect of Nightmare's 
Steelcage is backfiring.

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:44.540
Then Paralyzing Chain!

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:47.580
When an effect that sends 
cards from the opponent's deck

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:50.580
to the graveyard activates, 
it deals 300 points of damage!

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:03.230
Forgive me, Yusei.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:14.020
You seem pretty tired.  Will you last 
before your life points run out?

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:16.770
My turn.

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:20.010
That's the spirit, hero.

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:32.130
I'll now say goodbye to this place.

00:05:34.570 --> 00:05:39.650
If I leave my friends behind, 
I'll never truly be free.

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:45.850
Why did you have to say that?

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:53.810
I set three cards.

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:56.970
The Quick-Play Spell Psychic Cyclone!

00:05:56.970 --> 00:06:01.220
With this card, I declare whether 
a set card is a spell or a trap.

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:07.550
If I'm correct, that card is destroyed, 
and I get to draw one card.

00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:12.520
I'm going to select…  Let's see...

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:16.170
The very left card!

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:18.120
That's a trap card!

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:19.290
What?

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:27.050
It was Dust Tornado.  Too bad for you.

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:31.350
A trap card cannot activate 
on the turn it was set.

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:39.210
If you destroyed Poison Chain with that 
card, you still would've had a chance.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:44.030
That punk's instincts are working 
well at this crucial time.

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:48.640
Due to the effect of Psychic 
Cyclone, I draw one card.

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:51.470
I set one more card.

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:53.640
I end my turn.

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:56.560
My turn!

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:00.760
I summon Iron Chain Blaster!

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:09.350
Due to Poison Chain's effect, you send 
cards in your deck to the graveyard

00:07:09.350 --> 00:07:12.050
equal to the total Level 
of my Chain Monsters.

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:16.500
Discard 12 cards!

00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:24.320
Your deck has 6 cards left.

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:29.920
If you have no cards left to 
draw during your turn, you lose!

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:34.100
Furthermore, due to 
Paralyzing Chain's effect,

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:37.500
when you send cards in your 
deck to the graveyard,

00:07:37.500 --> 00:07:39.500
you take 300 points of damage.

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:44.280
I activate Iron Chain 
Blaster's monster effect!

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:47.460
I send Iron Chain Snake to the graveyard.

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:49.710
Fire!

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:56.440
Due to this, you take an 
additional 800 points of damage.

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:59.640
Then due to Iron Chain 
Repairman's monster effect,

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:03.280
I Special Summon a Level 4-or-below 
Chain Monster from my graveyard.

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:07.940
This is bad.

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:11.400
At this rate, Yusei will lose 
against his looping effect.

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:13.880
I end my turn.

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:18.530
Your Nightmare's Steelcage 
vanishes this turn.

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:26.920
It seems you lost your fighting spirit.

00:08:27.140 --> 00:08:30.250
I'm willing to accept your surrender.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.680
Is that all you have to say?

00:08:35.670 --> 00:08:39.480
As you wish, I'll send you to hell!

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:41.160
My turn.

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:45.500
What?  What's going on?

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:49.010
What happened?

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:50.220
I don't know.

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:53.080
However, there's nothing wrong now.

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:55.830
It was just a blackout.

00:08:57.760 --> 00:09:01.380
He successfully escaped.

00:09:02.090 --> 00:09:06.560
Make sure you escape.  I'll 
buy the time you need.

00:09:06.950 --> 00:09:08.490
I'll continue the duel.

00:09:08.570 --> 00:09:11.710
I activate the trap Jar of Greed.

00:09:12.010 --> 00:09:14.440
I draw one card.

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:17.310
You intentionally decreased the 
number of cards in your deck?

00:09:17.310 --> 00:09:20.590
Now you only have four cards 
remaining in your deck.

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:24.100
The trap card Call of the Haunted.

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:28.120
With this card, I Special Summon a monster 
from my graveyard in attack position.

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:31.040
Resurrect, The Kick Man.

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:37.000
Even if you resurrect that worthless 
card, nothing is going to change.

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:42.600
When The Kick Man is Special Summoned, it 
can equip an Equip Card in the graveyard.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:44.840
A card in the graveyard?

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:51.790
Among the cards that you forced me to 
discard is a card with infinite potential!

00:09:52.120 --> 00:09:55.400
I equip Axe of Despair on to The Kick Man!

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:01.400
All right!  The Kick Man 
gains 1000 attack points.

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:05.010
Then I summon Exiled Force!

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:09.670
The Kick Man attacks Iron Chain Snake.

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:20.120
Check out his bad acting.

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:22.750
No, there's something different.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:29.170
Exiled Force, attack the 
other Iron Chain Snake!

00:10:29.210 --> 00:10:32.990
No!  Wait a second!

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:45.320
No way…  Why is their electricity 
flowing through my Duel Disk?

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:07.030
There's a trespasser in the 
electric maintenance room.

00:11:07.030 --> 00:11:11.240
I repeat, there's a trespasser 
in the electric maintenance room.

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:14.190
A trespasser?

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:23.540
Chief!

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:26.490
We've brought the trespasser.

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:29.930
You…

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:35.470
How did you escape?

00:11:35.470 --> 00:11:36.500
Chief.

00:11:36.740 --> 00:11:39.170
There was a hole underneath his bed.

00:11:39.170 --> 00:11:41.010
You!

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:44.370
Hurry up and turn off the electricity 
flowing through my Duel Disk.

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:47.000
Sorry, but that's not possible.

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:49.350
What do you mean?

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:56.580
The system blocks has been destroyed, so it's 
impossible to turn off the electricity to the Duel Disk.

00:11:57.340 --> 00:12:03.620
After I get rid of this garbage 
from Satellite, I will kill you!

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:08.440
Say whatever you want because 
you won't beat Yusei.

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:12.040
Why did you come back?

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:13.880
It's just like you said.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:18.280
If I escape and leave my friends behind, 
then there will be shackles my heart.

00:12:18.490 --> 00:12:22.880
Even if I live like that, 
I will never truly be free.

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:31.300
If you're personally going to judge his crime, 
then I'm adding a new stipulation to this duel.

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:36.100
If I win, you will ignore his escape attempt.

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:38.010
Yusei.

00:12:38.200 --> 00:12:39.410
Fine.

00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:44.000
But if you lose, he's going down with you!

00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:46.850
Let's continue the duel.

00:12:46.850 --> 00:12:53.120
I release Exiled Force to 
destroy Iron Chain Repairman.

00:12:55.990 --> 00:12:57.670
I end my turn.

00:12:57.700 --> 00:13:00.720
All right.  On the next 
turn, he will only lose

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:03.720
three cards due to the 
effect of Poison Chain.

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:07.140
He's hanging on by the skin of his neck.

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:09.790
But he can't let his guard down.

00:13:09.790 --> 00:13:15.510
If he summons a monster on the next 
turn, then he will lose four cards.

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:18.410
That means Yusei loses.

00:13:20.670 --> 00:13:22.980
My turn!

00:13:25.390 --> 00:13:29.260
It's not a monster.  You're lucky.

00:13:29.500 --> 00:13:35.560
But that doesn't matter.  I know everything that 
you've been planning to do since the very beginning.

00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:41.550
This detention center is my field.

00:13:41.780 --> 00:13:45.930
Thanks to the security cameras, I've 
known your cards from the start.

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:50.370
Your set cards are two trap cards.

00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:55.640
The right one is Taunt, which 
can't activate this turn.

00:13:55.930 --> 00:14:01.660
The left one is Battle Mania, 
which forces monsters to battle.

00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:07.880
It's disadvantageous for me to fight his 
monster that's powered up with Axe of Despair.

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:12.080
I have to get rid of Battle Mania.

00:14:12.520 --> 00:14:16.360
I activate the spell card Reload!

00:14:16.890 --> 00:14:19.050
I add my hand to my deck.

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:23.420
Then I draw the same number 
of cards that I returned!

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:32.810
The spell card Mystical Space Typhoon.

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:36.600
With this, I destroy the 
left card on your field.

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:38.440
Activate!

00:14:40.970 --> 00:14:43.450
What?  It's not Battle Mania?

00:14:43.450 --> 00:14:45.620
At this moment, I activate my trap.

00:14:45.620 --> 00:14:47.260
Battle Mania.

00:14:47.790 --> 00:14:53.110
Due to the effect of this trap, monsters 
on the field must battle this turn!

00:14:54.220 --> 00:14:59.190
Well done.  Poison Chain's effect can 
only be used when he doesn't battle.

00:14:59.220 --> 00:15:01.700
If he battles, it can't activate.

00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:06.330
What's going on?  The set card has changed.

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:09.510
That should have been the 
location of the set card.

00:15:09.510 --> 00:15:13.850
He probably changed the 
order during that blackout.

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:16.880
I can't let my guard down against him.

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:19.940
However, no matter what he 
does, his life is still over.

00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:22.790
I'll show you how scary this deck is.

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:26.470
I summon Iron Chain Coil!

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:33.370
Iron Chain Coil tunes Iron Chain Blaster.

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:35.100
Synchro Summon.

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:37.670
Appear, Iron Chain Dragon!

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:49.690
Until the end of the turn, for every Chain 
Monster in my graveyard that I remove from play,

00:15:49.690 --> 00:15:52.200
Iron Chain Dragon gains 200 attack points.

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:55.190
There are five Chain 
Monsters in my graveyard!

00:15:55.190 --> 00:15:59.310
Therefore, Iron Chain Dragon 
gains 1000 attack points!

00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:05.530
3500 attack points.

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:07.800
Go, Iron Chain Dragon!

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:09.990
Chain Blast!

00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:19.070
Iron Chain Dragon's new 
monster effect activates!

00:16:19.070 --> 00:16:24.510
When this card attacks, you have to send 
three cards in your deck to the graveyard!

00:16:27.940 --> 00:16:32.470
Then due to the Paralyzing Chain, 
you take 300 points of damage!

00:16:39.860 --> 00:16:40.990
Yusei!

00:16:41.150 --> 00:16:42.120
Yusei!

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:43.560
Bro!

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:46.960
I end my turn.

00:16:58.000 --> 00:16:59.720
My turn.

00:17:07.950 --> 00:17:11.430
You only have 100 life points 
remaining and one card in your hand.

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:13.430
There are zero cards in your deck!

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:15.880
And you have no set cards.

00:17:16.120 --> 00:17:19.010
This battle is over.

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:22.440
Yeah.  This battle is over.

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:25.970
You lose.

00:17:26.210 --> 00:17:27.540
What?

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:33.980
Since you sent many cards to 
my graveyard, I'm going to win.

00:17:34.340 --> 00:17:37.050
You called us garbage.

00:17:37.170 --> 00:17:39.050
But you're wrong.

00:17:39.860 --> 00:17:45.820
This duel proves that no one 
in the world is useless.

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:53.900
I knew that you were spying on my 
hand with the security cameras.

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:58.790
That's why during the blackout, I 
changed how I held my special card

00:17:58.790 --> 00:18:01.790
so that the security cameras couldn't see it.

00:18:02.610 --> 00:18:07.000
When you learned that the information 
from the security cameras were wrong,

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:08.500
you should have been more careful.

00:18:11.430 --> 00:18:12.710
You punk!

00:18:12.710 --> 00:18:16.490
Here I go! From my hand, 
I summon Rubble King!

00:18:18.960 --> 00:18:23.000
With this card, when there are 
30 or more cards in my graveyard,

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:25.020
I can activate a trap from my hand!

00:18:25.550 --> 00:18:28.120
I activate this card.

00:18:28.360 --> 00:18:31.520
The trap card Blasting the Ruins.

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:39.430
When there are 30 or more cards in my 
graveyard, you take 3000 points of damage.

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:41.630
What?

00:19:01.090 --> 00:19:02.390
You did it, Yusei!

00:19:02.390 --> 00:19:03.980
Impressive, bro!

00:19:03.980 --> 00:19:05.860
That guy!

00:19:05.860 --> 00:19:07.130
He did it!

00:19:07.130 --> 00:19:11.070
Our cards defeated the chief!

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:19.190
Yusei!  Yusei!  Yusei!

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:23.310
Arrest him!

00:19:23.310 --> 00:19:24.260
What?

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:26.460
That's not what you promised!

00:19:26.460 --> 00:19:29.270
I don't recall making a promise with you!

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:32.010
Stop it, Chief Takasu.

00:19:33.750 --> 00:19:38.750
You're painful to watch.  
I observed the duel.

00:19:39.020 --> 00:19:43.470
It seems you do not have the 
skills to run this place.

00:19:43.470 --> 00:19:45.980
The person who's going to vanish is you.

00:20:00.890 --> 00:20:04.190
That's nice that you get to leave right away.

00:20:04.190 --> 00:20:08.100
Thank goodness that person named 
Godwin showed up when he did.

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:12.480
You're right.  It looks like 
we can leave here soon too.

00:20:12.550 --> 00:20:19.050
Since that guy showed up here personally, 
he must be interested in you.

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:25.880
Bro, I have a farewell gift for you.

00:20:26.790 --> 00:20:27.890
But this is…

00:20:27.890 --> 00:20:34.010
It's fine.  You'll use 
it better than me, bro.

00:20:35.820 --> 00:20:37.910
I'll take care of it.

00:20:38.010 --> 00:20:41.620
Yusei, take this card.

00:20:41.830 --> 00:20:46.080
At a store downtown named Bootleg, 
there's a man named Saiga.

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:49.380
If you show him this, he'll help you.

00:20:50.510 --> 00:20:51.920
Thank you.

00:20:54.390 --> 00:20:56.520
Is this fine?

00:20:56.710 --> 00:20:59.680
To let him go free?

00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:09.200
There's no other choice.  His Signer power 
wouldn't awaken if he remained inside.

00:21:09.350 --> 00:21:14.320
Besides, I didn't say I 
would let him go free.

00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:17.850
Then we need a trap.

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:38.820
He's coming out.

00:21:43.150 --> 00:21:49.790
You will pay for this scar!

00:22:05.740 --> 00:22:11.320
What can we grasp?  What can we do?

00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:16.710
We'll step forward and find out

00:22:17.090 --> 00:22:22.640
My unstoppable emotions, the 
beating of my passionate heart

00:22:22.800 --> 00:22:27.880
I heard the voice of truth

00:22:28.070 --> 00:22:31.040
After I was hurt, I learned

00:22:33.610 --> 00:22:36.630
Of a place where I can become stronger

00:22:38.580 --> 00:22:43.790
I stack my dreams in my palm

00:22:43.920 --> 00:22:49.190
And I'll someday pass them to you

00:22:49.620 --> 00:22:55.130
Seeking for the signal 
to start, my soul roars

00:22:55.430 --> 00:23:00.470
I will overcome my suffocating 
and mediocre life

00:23:01.030 --> 00:23:06.560
I'll dash and acquire all the bright futures

00:23:06.710 --> 00:23:15.980
Carrying the bonds I believe 
in, I run towards tomorrow
